# 1️⃣ Database Partitioning

# Big Idea

Partitioning means:

```text id="m5t8i3"
Split one huge table into smaller parts
```

But logically it still feels like one table.

---

# Mental Model 🧠

Imagine a huge library.

Without partitioning:

```text id="8g9y7j"
All books in one giant room ❌
```

Hard to search.

With partitioning:

```text id="ik6r1m"
Books split by category/floor ✅
```

Much faster.

---

# Why Partitioning is Needed

Suppose table has:

```text id="k0j0we"
1 billion rows
```

Searching entire table is slow.

Partitioning reduces search area.

---

# Types of Partitioning

---

## 🔹 Range Partitioning

Split by ranges.

Example:

```text id="d6j4q8"
2023 data → Partition A
2024 data → Partition B
2025 data → Partition C
```

Very common.

---

## 🔹 List Partitioning

Split by categories.

Example:

```text id="dlfz0o"
CSE students → one partition
ECE students → another
```

---

## 🔹 Hash Partitioning

Database automatically distributes rows using hash function.

Used for balancing load.

---

# Example Query Benefit

Without partitioning:

```text id="9m3u6f"
Scan all years
```

With partitioning:

```text id="83d5u6"
Only scan 2025 partition
```

Huge speed improvement.

---

# Python Analogy 🧠

Without partitioning:

```python id="b98k8m"
all_data = huge_list
```

With partitioning:

```python id="d72g2w"
data_2024 = []
data_2025 = []
```

Search smaller lists.

---

# Memory Trick 🧠

```text id="0b2zme"
Partitioning = divide one huge table
```

