# 2️⃣ Sharding & Replication

Now scaling across multiple machines.

---

# 🔹 Sharding

## Big Idea

Sharding means:

```text id="j3h8z6"
Split database across multiple servers
```

---

# Mental Model 🧠

One shop cannot handle all customers.

Open multiple branches.

---

# Example

Server 1:

```text id="v4go6j"
Users A–M
```

Server 2:

```text id="q1e6zn"
Users N–Z
```

Load distributed.

---

# Why Sharding Helps

✔ Handles massive traffic
✔ Improves scalability
✔ Reduces server load

---

# Challenge ⚠️

Queries across shards become harder.

Example:

* joins
* transactions

More complex.

---

# Python Analogy

```python id="gh0pxz"
server1_users = [...]
server2_users = [...]
```

Data distributed.

---

# Memory Trick 🧠

```text id="l8n8b0"
Sharding = split across servers
```

---

# 🔹 Replication

## Big Idea

Replication means:

```text id="v69u9u"
Copy same database to multiple servers
```

---

# Why?

If one server crashes:

```text id="0t4s6n"
Another copy still available ✅
```

Improves reliability.

---

# Types

---

## Primary-Replica

Primary:

```text id="38avdi"
Handles writes
```

Replicas:

```text id="7e6b4e"
Handle reads
```

Very common architecture.

---

# Benefits

✔ High availability
✔ Faster reads
✔ Backup safety

---

# Problem ⚠️

Replication delay can occur.

Replica may not instantly update.

---

# Sharding vs Replication

| Feature | Sharding         | Replication |
| ------- | ---------------- | ----------- |
| Goal    | Scale data       | Copy data   |
| Data    | Different pieces | Same copy   |
| Benefit | Scalability      | Reliability |

---

# Easy Visual

```text id="h9dd4j"
Sharding:
Different data on different servers

Replication:
Same data copied everywhere
```

---

# 🔥 Placement Insight

Very common questions:

